;; deepcreekfieldguide.com — DNS zone file
;;
;; Import at: Cloudflare → deepcreekfieldguide.com → DNS → Records
;;            → Import and Export → Import DNS records → upload this file
;;
;; DO IT IN THIS ORDER:
;;
;;   1. Import. Cloudflare imports records PROXIED (orange) by default — switch
;;      all five to DNS only (grey) before going any further. Proxying before
;;      GitHub has issued its certificate is what causes the infinite redirect
;;      loop.
;;
;;   2. GitHub → repo Settings → Pages → Custom domain →
;;      deepcreekfieldguide.com → Save. Wait for the green tick; usually a few
;;      minutes, occasionally an hour.
;;
;;   3. Tick "Enforce HTTPS" on that same page. It stays greyed out until the
;;      certificate exists.
;;
;;   4. Only now, if you want Cloudflare's CDN: switch the four apex A records
;;      and www back to Proxied (orange), then set
;;      SSL/TLS → Overview → FULL (STRICT). Not Flexible.
;;
;;   5. With the proxy on: turn OFF Auto Minify and Rocket Loader, and add a
;;      Cache Rule bypassing cache for *.html — Cloudflare will otherwise serve
;;      stale pages after every deploy.
;;
;; The four A records are GitHub Pages' published apex addresses.
;; https://docs.github.com/en/pages/configuring-a-custom-domain-for-your-github-pages-site

$ORIGIN deepcreekfieldguide.com.
$TTL 3600

;; Apex → GitHub Pages
@	3600	IN	A	185.199.108.153
@	3600	IN	A	185.199.109.153
@	3600	IN	A	185.199.110.153
@	3600	IN	A	185.199.111.153

;; www → the GitHub Pages host (NOT the apex, and not the repo path)
www	3600	IN	CNAME	werth-code.github.io.

;; No mail on this domain. These two say so publicly, which stops the domain
;; being used to spoof mail from you. Remove them if you ever add email.
@	3600	IN	TXT	"v=spf1 -all"
_dmarc	3600	IN	TXT	"v=DMARC1; p=reject; rua=mailto:matthewwerth@gmail.com"
